{"book":"equations","bookTitle":"Equations and inequalities","concept":3,"title":"Two-step equations","grades":"Grade 7","goal":"I can solve two-step equations.","teach":"In 2x + 3 = 11, x is first multiplied by 2, then 3 is added. Undo these in <b>reverse order</b>: first subtract 3, then divide by 2. 2x + 3 = 11 → 2x = 8 → x = 4.","tvis":"<div class=\"vis\"><span class=\"vi\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" style=\"width:315px;height:auto\" viewBox=\"0 0 242 44\"><rect x=\"2.0\" y=\"2.0\" width=\"50.0\" height=\"40.0\" fill=\"#E3D6CE\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"27.0\" y=\"27.0\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#444444\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\">x</text><rect x=\"58.0\" y=\"2.0\" width=\"60.0\" height=\"40.0\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"88.0\" y=\"27.0\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#444444\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\">× 2</text><rect x=\"124.0\" y=\"2.0\" width=\"60.0\" height=\"40.0\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"154.0\" y=\"27.0\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#444444\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\">+ 3</text><rect x=\"190.0\" y=\"2.0\" width=\"50.0\" height=\"40.0\" fill=\"#E3D6CE\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"215.0\" y=\"27.0\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#444444\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\">11</text></svg></span><div class=\"cap\">Undo in reverse: 11 − 3 = 8, then 8 ÷ 2 = 4.</div></div>","ex":{"q":"Solve 5x − 4 = 21.","steps":["Add 4 to both sides: 5x = 25.","Divide both sides by 5: x = 5.","Check: 5 × 5 − 4 = 21. <span style=\"font-family:'TeX Gyre Pagella'\">✓</span>"]},"watch":"Undo the + or − first, then the × or ÷.","qs":[{"text":"Solve 4y − 5 = 23.","vis":"","parts":[{"t":"box","label":"y","a":"7","form":"val","o":null}],"hint":"4y = 28","steps":"1. Rule (balance method): do the same to both sides. Undo each operation with its inverse (− undoes +, ÷ undoes ×): first undo + or −, then undo × or ÷.<br>2. Add 5: 4y = 28<br>3. Divide by 4: y = 7"},{"text":"Solve <span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\"><i>x</i></span><span class=\"d\">2</span></span> + 3 = 10.","vis":"","parts":[{"t":"box","label":"x","a":"14","form":"val","o":null}],"hint":"<span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\"><i>x</i></span><span class=\"d\">2</span></span> = 7","steps":"1. Rule (balance method): do the same to both sides. Undo each operation with its inverse (− undoes +, ÷ undoes ×): first undo + or −, then undo × or ÷.<br>2. Subtract 3: x ÷ 2 = 7<br>3. Multiply by 2: x = 14"},{"text":"Solve 6 + 5m = 41.","vis":"","parts":[{"t":"box","label":"m","a":"7","form":"val","o":null}],"hint":"5m = 35","steps":"1. Rule (balance method): do the same to both sides. Undo each operation with its inverse (− undoes +, ÷ undoes ×): first undo + or −, then undo × or ÷.<br>2. Subtract 6: 5m = 35<br>3. Divide by 5: m = 7"}]}